[block
  'ORD-0032-stores'
  [ctx
    'the spec of EMS-002'
    '.guidelines/.orders/EMS-002/EMS-002.pgml'
  [/ctx]
  [ctx
    'questions 10 and 11 of the EMS-001 return'
    '.guidelines/.orders/EMS-001/RETURN.md'
  [/ctx]
  [tgt
    'behind engine=relay the page holds no store of its own: it receives the tables of the engine once, at load, and a request carries only the templates that differ from the stores of the engine, named by their digest, as the Regent decided on 2026-10-21'
  [/tgt]
  [ctx
    'the Regent, 2026-10-21: on the tables, yes, do that, in place of classify answered from the JS tables of the page, which contradicts Glyph 100% in Rust; on the templates, c seems more consistent, follow it'
  [/ctx]
  [ctx
    'measured at 06e8de3: the tables, classify and the template list of the page come from its JS files, so a machine whose stores differ is read two ways on one screen; useTemplates stays on the JS core, so a template the user saves expands on the JS path and reaches no engine behind the relay; the page reads 15 tables and VERSION, and classify reads 2 more, ELEMENT_INPUT and the blend rows of the rules'
  [/ctx]
  [cnst
    'one ORD for both, because what differs can only be told against the templates of the engine, and the tables bring them'
  [/cnst]
  [cnst
    'tables is a call of the protocol: VERSION, the 15 tables the page reads, ELEMENT_INPUT, BLENDS, the blend rows of the rules in store order, and templates, the map of the engine; the JS first, the Rust byte for byte, and the installed engine answers from the stores of its machine'
  [/cnst]
  [cnst
    'a request may carry differ, a digest and the templates: the digest is ck of the JSON text of the templates, and the engine lays them over its own for that request; a digest that does not match and a shape that is not one are thrown, never guessed'
  [/cnst]
  [cnst
    'in the page only the transport changes, and classify makes no request; no call falls to the JS behind the relay, so a page whose engine does not answer throws'
  [/cnst]
  [cmp
    'the tables'
    'tables answers the same bytes in both engines, and the installed engine answers the templates of its machine'
    [ctx[/ctx]
    [cnst[/cnst]
  [/cmp]
